#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_gamma_regularized

#% text
# `inverse_gamma_regularized(a, s)` gives the `x` with `gamma_regularized(a, x) = s`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For `a > 0` and `0 < s < 1` there is one solution `x > 0`; `s = 1` gives 0.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% item
# `inverse_gamma_regularized` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_gamma_regularized(2.0, 0.5)
#% output
#= 1.6783469900166605

#% cell
inverse_gamma_regularized(0.5, 0.1)
#% output
#= 1.3527717270477073

#% cell
inverse_gamma_regularized(10.0, 0.95)
#% output
#= 5.425405697091294

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The 95% point of the chi-square distribution with 3 degrees of freedom:

#% cell
2*inverse_gamma_regularized(1.5, 0.05)
#% output
#= 7.81472790325118

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `gamma_regularized` undoes it:

#% cell
gamma_regularized(3.5, inverse_gamma_regularized(3.5, 0.25))
#% output
#= 0.24999999999999997

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `gamma_regularized`, `inverse_beta_regularized`, `gamma_distribution`, `quantile`
